;; =============================================================================
;; Spec: Ariadne step 2d — enforce grants on PR merge
;; =============================================================================

{:spec/title "Require granted, transacted PR merges"

 :spec/description
 "Finish the PR-merge half of Ariadne step 2d. The existing merge transaction
  already records a durable proposal and reconciles GitHub state, but it still
  commits with :authority/unenforced. At the effect-decision seam, request a
  narrowly scoped :effect/merge grant, evaluate it with the decision kernel,
  and commit using the resulting grant and DecisionEnvelope identifiers.

  Preserve the honesty behavior already delivered: enabling auto-merge is a
  committing state, not a merged claim, and the merge SHA comes from GitHub
  reconciliation rather than local HEAD. Decompose the current nested merge
  flow into named domain decisions and application steps before adding grant
  enforcement. The require-no-unresolved-threads policy must use provider
  readback instead of its current always-clear stub."

 :spec/intent
 {:type :feature
  :scope ["components/pr-lifecycle/**"]}

 :spec/constraints
 ["No GitHub merge command runs without an active matching grant and allow-class envelope"
  "The durable proposal is the authority recheck input at commit"
  "Enabling auto-merge is not reported as a completed merge"
  "Published merge SHAs come from GitHub reconciliation, never local HEAD"
  "Provider reads, domain decisions, and effect orchestration remain separate"
  "Repeated proposal, grant, and envelope maps use shared test factories"
  "Functions must express one decision or orchestration step without nested control pyramids"
  "Stratified design permits at most three layers per implementation namespace"]

 :spec/acceptance-criteria
 ["A merge without an active :effect/merge grant fires no gh merge command"
  "A mismatched or expired merge grant fires no gh merge command"
  "A valid merge records grant and DecisionEnvelope identifiers before gh invocation"
  "Enabling auto-merge leaves the effect in :committing until reconciliation"
  "The merged event is published only after reconcile! observes a GitHub merge"
  "The published merge SHA equals GitHub's reconciled mergeCommit"
  "The unresolved-thread policy denies a merge when GitHub reports an unresolved thread"
  "poly check reports 0 errors and 0 warnings"
  "full bb test is green"]

 :spec/priority
 {:tier :high
  :axes #{:correctness :observation :governance-credibility}
  :theme :ariadne-grants
  :rationale "Merge remains an ambient-authority escape hatch until the delivered transaction requires its grant."
  :blocks []
  :blocked-by ["ariadne-grant-issuance.spec.edn"]}

 :spec/workflow-type :canonical-sdlc}
